<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cajamarca</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cajamarca is a city in the northern highlands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>, capital of the Cajamarca region. An <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-empire">Inca</a> administrative centre with baths and temples, it was where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-pizarro">Francisco Pizarro</a> and his small Spanish force ambushed the Inca emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atahualpa">Atahualpa</a> on 16 November 1532, capturing him and killing many of his retinue. Atahualpa offered a huge ransom in gold and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> but was executed there in 1533.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cajamarca.jpg" alt="Cajamarca" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SrDingleberry69 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Catedral_de_Cajamarca_Per%C3%BA.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
